# Klyte Kanban usage

## Default

Do **not** work with Kanban tasks, sprints, epics, backlog, or the board unless the user **explicitly** asks.

Under `.klyte-kanban/`, agents may **only** read and write files in **`RefsLibrary/`** (reference docs beyond board scope). Do **not** open, create, or edit other `.klyte-kanban/` paths (tasks, sprints, archive, board files, etc.) by hand — those go through MCP when board work is requested.

## How to call Kanban

When Kanban **is** requested, use the **user-klyte-kanban MCP** tools only (`kk_workspace`, `kk_task`, `kk_sprint`, `kk_backlog`, `kk_epic`, `kk_batch`).

**Never** invoke Kanban via the shell / CLI / “line command” (or any non-MCP wrapper) as a substitute for those tools.

## Commits from MCP

When a `kk_*` response includes a non-empty **`commitMessage`**, **always create a git commit** using that message (stage the relevant product / board changes as appropriate). Do not skip or defer it.

If MCP already auto-committed, do not duplicate the commit; still verify status. If auto-commit failed or was off and `commitMessage` is present, commit yourself with that message.

## If MCP is insufficient

**Stop immediately.** Tell the user what was needed, which `kk_*` tool(s) were tried, and what is missing or broken. Ask for help — do **not** invent workarounds (CLI, editing kanban files by hand, etc.) unless the user explicitly directs that.
